 "title": "Epiphany",
 "dates": "Friday, January 1 – Monday, January 11, 2010",
 "logline": "The last days of Christmas break and the first day back: a long cord into a pantry, a letter in block capitals, a sign in eyeliner at an airport — and a gas station where something goes public.",
 "previously": [
  {
   "text": "On the bluff before Christmas, Skye: “When you get back, we’re dating. Officially.” … “I’ll make it a whole thing.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At Trumbull, while your mother showed your father the machines, Danny: “Third’s Ma’s Sunday. You’re still home.” “Till the ninth.” “Don’t let him sit in the truck.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "From behind the register at her father’s market, Lena: “Julian lands tomorrow at four.” … “I won’t call as much this week.” “I know.” … “…I’ll call.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "Half past one in the morning, on the phone in the basement: “Monday,” Skye says. “Not asking. Telling.”"
  },
  {
   "text": "At your midnight you answered Skye first, on purpose. At hers, the second the clock turned: *Happy New Year, Jack. —L.* You wrote back *happy new year lena*, and said a Hail Mary for her in the cold.",
   "if": "s2e2_newyear==\"sincerity\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At your midnight you answered Skye first, on purpose. At hers, the second the clock turned: *Happy New Year, Jack. —L.* You typed *1:00. not 1:01. i saw.* — and erased it.",
   "if": "s2e2_newyear==\"almost\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At your midnight you answered Skye first, on purpose. At hers, the second the clock turned: *Happy New Year, Jack. —L.* You sent back a joke about your father and a firework.",
   "if": "s2e2_newyear==\"wit\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At your midnight you answered Skye first, on purpose. At hers, the second the clock turned: *Happy New Year, Jack. —L.* You left it for the morning.",
   "if": "s2e2_newyear==\"restraint\""
  },
  {
   "text": "At your midnight you answered Skye first, on purpose. At hers, the second the clock turned: *Happy New Year, Jack. —L.*",
   "if": "!s2e2_newyear"
  }
 ],
